Site-local hooks and configuration for the container stack on our FreeBSD
hosts:

* OCI createRuntime/poststop hooks:
    - apt-cache-start, which seeds APT::Cache-Start into Linux container root
      filesystems, working around the FreeBSD Linuxulator not implementing
      mremap(2) growth, so stock Debian and Ubuntu images can run apt-get
      without the per-distro "_fix" base images;
    - children, linprocfs and zfs, which apply the org.freebsd.jail.* and
      zfs.dataset podman annotations to the jail once it exists.
  Annotation-gated hooks are inert on hosts that never set the annotation, so
  all four ship everywhere.
* registries.conf.d trust for the LAN registry, so pulls and pushes work
  against the LAN registry without --tls-verify=false;
* the CNI network configuration that gives containers a real LAN address
  through the epair plugin.

Config files that differ per host are installed as .sample, so local edits
survive upgrades; run the port's tcreech-enable-hooks-dir helper once per
host,
because containers.conf has no drop-in directory for the hooks_dir key.
